  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nCurrently I see no obvious way to keep myself up-to-date regarding the ever-changing HTML spec. Preferably there were some regular release notes (monthly or quarterly) for web developers to follow, including new features that are being added, major changes, or major changes on the user agent side which are relevant (for example major browsers shipping a new HTML feature).\n\nPerhaps this information exists somewhere in some form, in that case it would be great if a link to this information could be added to the standard's home page.\n\nIt would be even more awesome if something like semantic versioning could be introduced, although I'm not sure how realistic would it be to have some \"regular\" releases if there is even such a thing for HTML.",
